cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use florilegium in your work, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: florilegium
abstract: >-
  Procedurally generated Delft-blue floral page margins for LuaLaTeX. Every petal, leaf
  and stem is a parametric curve computed in Lua while the page is written, and placed by a
  greedy space-filling layout that grows plants to fit the free space on each page. The
  plants and their visitors are species sampled from genomes of botanical traits, and a
  TikZ library draws the same species as pics, in pure TikZ under pdfLaTeX or through Lua
  under LuaLaTeX.
authors:
  - family-names: Raymond
    given-names: Kevin
repository-code: https://github.com/kevinraymond/florilegium
url: https://kevinraymond.github.io/florilegium/
license:
  - MIT
  - LPPL-1.3c
keywords:
  - LaTeX
  - LuaLaTeX
  - Lua
  - TikZ
  - pdfLaTeX
  - generative art
  - procedural generation
  - typography
  - ornament
